file_merger: TSV lines may end in CRLF (checkpoint 2)

Sentence: "TSV: ... `\n` line endings". The hidden fixtures are written by csv.DictWriter,
whose default line terminator is `\r\n`, so every TSV input ends its lines in CRLF while the
spec promises `\n`. Both min11-ABDFJKMN runs hand-parse TSV (the spec forbids quoting) and
strip only `\n`, so the last column of every TSV keeps a `\r` and the merged output grows a
phantom column. The reference solution strips `\r\n`. Tests: tsv_empty_fields, tsv_gzip,
tsv_whitespace_values, unicode_tsv, consensus_type_tie, five_file_mixed, four_format_merge,
auto_mix_union, consensus_inference (nine, every case with a TSV input, all from checkpoint 2).

